**Related Spec**: specs/67-bake-authored-materials-to-contract-compliant-uv-texture-sets/

# File: tests/blender/test_bake_unique.py, tests/blender/test_variants.py, tests/blender/test_contract_validate.py
# Generated from: specs/142-fix-naming-collisions-that-pass-validate-and-fail-after-the-bake/requirements.md
Feature: Naming collisions are resolved before they fail a finalize run

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Bake outputs take the contract names when source images already hold them
    Given a Crate whose authored material samples images named T_Crate_Body_BC, T_Crate_Body_N, and T_Crate_Body_ORM
    When the bake step runs
    Then the baked material samples images named exactly T_Crate_Body_BC, T_Crate_Body_N, and T_Crate_Body_ORM
    And the full contract reports no naming.texture finding after the variants step

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Authored materials keep their source images
    Given the same Crate after the bake
    When the retired M_Crate_Body_Authoring material is inspected
    Then it samples the original image datablocks, now named T_Crate_Body_BC_Src, T_Crate_Body_N_Src, and T_Crate_Body_ORM_Src
    And their pixels are unchanged

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Re-running the bake leaves no suffixed contract images
    Given a Crate that was already baked
    When the bake step runs again
    Then exactly one image holds each contract name
    And no image name matches a contract name followed by .NNN

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Export names mesh datablocks after their objects
    Given a Crate part SM_Crate_Seat whose mesh data is named SM_Crate_Seat.001
    When the export step writes the Desktop and Mobile FBX files
    Then re-importing each FBX shows every mesh named the same as its object
    And the session's object and mesh names are unchanged after export

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Shared mesh data is reported before the bake
    Given two Crate parts that share one mesh datablock
    When validate runs with authored=True
    Then it reports naming.mesh_data naming both parts and the datablock
    And the remediation says to make the mesh data single-user

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Assets without collisions are unchanged
    Given a Crate with neither collision
    When validate, bake, and export run
    Then the findings, image names, material names, and FBX file names are the same as before the fix
